1. What you may do without separate permission

You may:

- view, download, and study the source code;
- make local copies, branches, commits, patches, and modifications;
- build and run KubeVS for personal use, evaluation, testing, education, and
  development;
- create a GitHub fork when its primary purpose is preparing and submitting a
  contribution to the official KubeVS repository;
- submit issues, patches, and pull requests to the official repository; and
- use, modify, publish, and sell scripts, recipes, configuration, or other
  project files that you create with KubeVS.

A contribution fork must retain this license and copyright notice. It may not
publish KubeVS releases, offer KubeVS as a product or service, or present itself
as the official project.

2. What requires written permission

You need prior written permission from the copyright holder to:

- maintain or publish a fork for a purpose other than contributing changes back;
- distribute KubeVS source code or compiled binaries outside an allowed
  contribution fork;
- publish a modified version, derivative product, mirror, or unofficial release;
- use KubeVS or a substantial part of it in a commercial product or paid
  service;
- sublicense, sell, rent, or resell KubeVS; or
- use KubeVS branding, logos, or names in a way that suggests endorsement or
  official status.

Permission may be recorded in a GitHub issue, pull request, or another written
message from the copyright holder. Permission may include additional conditions.

3. Contributions

You keep copyright in your original contribution. By intentionally submitting a
patch or pull request to the official KubeVS repository, you grant the copyright
holder a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use,
reproduce, modify, distribute, sublicense, and relicense that contribution as
part of KubeVS.

You confirm that you have the right to submit the contribution and that it does
not knowingly violate another person's rights. Accepting a contribution does
not grant permission to distribute the rest of KubeVS outside this license.

4. Generated output and user projects

This license does not claim ownership of KubeJS scripts, recipes, configuration,
assets, or other project content created by a user with KubeVS. Those files
belong to their respective authors, subject to any third-party rights they
